# Migration files are hashed byte-for-byte by sqlx and embedded in the binary at compile
# time. If git rewrites their line endings, every checksum changes and the app refuses to
# start against any database that was migrated before the rewrite: "migration N was
# previously applied but has been modified". Pin them to LF everywhere so the bytes sqlx
# hashes are the bytes that stay in the repo.
*.sql text eol=lf
